      "method": "actual_pixels_view_image",
      "observations": "The actual image shows inverse kinematics, desired velocity J^-1(Theta) times desired Cartesian velocity, and a two-term acceleration product rule with a dot on the inverse-Jacobian factor. For exact differentiation of a selected desired IK branch, the evaluation must be along that branch; using actual Theta is a different resolved-rate interpretation unless actual and desired coincide. Ordinary inverse needs a square nonsingular Jacobian. Noise amplification and computational delay are explicit cautions."
    },
    {
      "physicalPage": 757,
      "slideId": "lectures-p0757",
      "previewPath": "sources/previews/lectures/page-0757.webp",
